# @hub-lanes

# ── LANE WAKE CALENDAR (BH-9074, BH-9067.2) ─────────────────────────────────
# Every minute. For each catalog/lane-calendar.d/<lane>.tsv line that matches
# one of the next LANE_WAKE_CALENDAR_LEAD_MIN minutes, one lwg_ring <lane>
# <scope> cal:<key> (the contract's bin/lib/lane-wake-gate.sh, #9122). A lane in
# wake mode off is not rung, and every mode is off until a settings row turns it
# on, so the lanes' own cron lines are unchanged. Without the gate lib the lane
# writes one line an hour and does nothing.
# Docs: docs/events-bh-9067/2-wake-pollers.bh-9074.md.
# Off: flags/lane-off-lane-wake-calendar (bin/harness-ctl.sh off lane-wake-calendar).
* * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && flock -n /root/harness/locks/lane-wake-calendar.lock /root/harness/bin/lane-wake-calendar.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
